<title>UK: Baltic, Black Sea crude exports fall, gas oil up.</title>
<headline>Baltic, Black Sea crude exports fall, gas oil up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exports of crude oil and refined oil products from Baltic and Black Sea terminals fell 38,563 barrels per day (bpd) in the second week of May to 2.089 million bpd, Petro-Logistics Ltd said.</p>
<p>The total was 114,945 bpd above the same week last year. The numbers for this year were mainly dragged down by a heavy fall in the amount of crude oil exported.</p>
<p>The Geneva-based consultancy, tracking tanker movements, said crude oil exports fell by 306,712 bpd on the week to 1,180,968 million bpd, 262,553 bpd below year-ago levels.</p>
<p>Gas oil exports almost doubled from the previous week. They were 231,287 bpd up to 460,952 bpd, 115,801 bpd higher than the same period last year.</p>
<p>Heavy fuel exports rose less sharply. They were up 29,122 bpd to 358,649 bpd, continuing a gradual recovery from low export numbers in April.</p>
<p>The following table provided by Petro Logistics is a breakdown of petroleum exports from the Baltics and the Black Sea in the second week of May.</p>
<p>			Crude     Fuel    Gas Oil     Naphtha  Mogas/Jet Total</p>
<p>FSU		 1,133,989   387,729  319,221    45,764     1,886,703</p>
<p>Romania/Bulgaria			   114,179    27,472	 141,651</p>
<p>TOTAL tonnes    1,133,989   387,729  433,400    73,236     2,028,354</p>
<p>TOTAL bpd	 1,180,968   358,649  460,952    88,929     2,089,498</p>
<p>Change week bpd  -306,712   +29,122 +231,287   -50,448    +58,188 -38,563</p>
<p>Change year bpd  -262,553   +34,495 +115,801   -29,381    +26,693 -114,945</p>
